WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:02.460
(host)
A snowstorm is one
weather phenomenon

00:00:02.544 --> 00:00:04.587
you don't want to
be surprised by.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.506
The same can be said
of the Yuki Onna,

00:00:06.589 --> 00:00:09.050
one of Japan's harshest
winter monsters.

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:12.512
This icy snow maiden might
steal your heart or your life.

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:14.389
She's beautiful and dangerous.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:16.725
The incarnation
of winter storms.

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:18.101
In some regions of Japan,

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.019
just catching a
glimpse of this figure

00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:22.522
will cause your soul
to leave your body.

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:24.816
Other places give her
the trait of motherhood.

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:26.693
She will ask you
to hold her baby

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:29.696
or may appear accompanied
by snow children.

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:32.741
And in some region stories,
she's a vengeful spirit,

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:35.076
actively seeking out
those who wronged her

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.453
when she was alive.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.288
[dramatic music]

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:41.583
I'm Dr. Emily Zarka,
and this is "Monstrum."

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:44.043
Many legends of the Yuki Onna

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:45.712
originate in the Tohoku region.

00:00:45.795 --> 00:00:47.839
Located in the mountainous
northeastern part

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:50.425
of the country known as
one of the coldest regions

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:51.760
of the island,

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:55.305
the area sees more snowfall
than any other region in Japan.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.599
The Yuki Onna is
identified by the blizzards

00:00:57.682 --> 00:01:01.394
she travels with as beautiful
and pale as the falling snow.

00:01:01.478 --> 00:01:03.521
She may have black
or white hair,

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:05.648
but it is always very long.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.984
Her thin tall body
can appear naked,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:12.363
but more often it is wrapped
in a blindingly white kimono.

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:14.657
Yuki Onna looks like a woman.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.619
So, many mistake
her for a ghost,

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:21.289
but she isn't the
spirit of a dead person.

00:01:21.372 --> 00:01:23.708
(Emily)
That's Hiroko Yoda,
author of the yokai book,

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:27.295
"Yokai Attack: The Japanese
Monster Survival Guide."

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:30.548
(Hiroko)
She is a yokai,
a living personification

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:32.884
of cold and winter.

00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:35.762
[ominous music]

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:45.647
But I don't consider
Yuki Onna a monster.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:49.734
I see her as
an avatar of nature.

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:54.280
The fact she's wearing a thin
kimono in such condition.

00:01:54.364 --> 00:01:58.701
It's strange, but the
white color, it's odd too.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:02.914
Of course, it's
symbolizes frost and snow.

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:07.794
[Yuki Onna speaking Japanese]

00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:11.589
But traditionally, white
kimono are also used

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:14.676
as a burial dress for the dead.

00:02:14.759 --> 00:02:18.137
It would be very
scary to see a woman

00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:22.100
dressed in a light white
kimono in a blizzard.

00:02:22.183 --> 00:02:24.894
(Emily)
She can shapeshift
into mist or falling snow.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:27.230
Making her invisible
against the blizzard

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.982
she appears alongside.

00:02:29.065 --> 00:02:31.693
The better to sneak up
on her victims.

00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:34.988
(Hiroko)
Yuki Onna's story
is a classic example.

00:02:35.071 --> 00:02:37.282
She tells us to never
underestimate

00:02:37.365 --> 00:02:39.409
the power of nature

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:44.414
and to be extra cautious
when going out in the winter,

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.625
especially into the wilderness.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:49.168
(Emily)
The Yuki Onna is a kind of

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:51.546
winter succubus-type yokai.

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:53.798
Stories tell of her
acts of seduction.

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:55.842
Encounters that always
end with her draining

00:02:55.925 --> 00:02:58.720
the life force of the men
she has relations with.

00:02:58.803 --> 00:03:02.181
More notoriously, however,
victims die of the cold

00:03:02.265 --> 00:03:03.892
either through exposure
to the elements

00:03:03.975 --> 00:03:06.019
or the woman's icy breath.

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:08.813
The snow woman first appears
in a collection of poetry

00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:11.816
written in the 15th century
by Sogi, a zen monk.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.068
He describes the Yuki Onna
he encountered

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:18.031
as tall and beautiful with
very pale skin and white hair.

00:03:18.114 --> 00:03:20.450
His experience is
accompanied by another tale

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.410
that would become one
of the most enduring

00:03:22.493 --> 00:03:24.162
versions of the Yuki Onna.

00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:25.246
The story of the woodcutter.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.166
Legend has it that while
cutting down trees,

00:03:28.249 --> 00:03:30.627
Minokichi and
his mentor Mosaku

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.795
were caught in
a horrible blizzard.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.923
Unable to cross
the river to return home,

00:03:35.006 --> 00:03:37.508
they seek shelter
in a boatman's hut.

00:03:37.592 --> 00:03:40.553
Later that night, Minokichi
wakes up freezing.

00:03:40.637 --> 00:03:42.305
Noticing the door
to the hut is open,

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.557
he turns to
his mentor and sees

00:03:44.641 --> 00:03:47.810
a stunningly beautiful
woman standing over him.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.854
She has extraordinarily
pale skin

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:52.148
and is wearing
a snow white kimono.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.776
She freezes the mentor
with her icy breath

00:03:54.859 --> 00:03:57.820
then turns her piercing
gaze to Minokichi,

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:00.907
but is immediately taken
by the man's own beauty.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.201
He was unusually handsome.

00:04:03.284 --> 00:04:05.453
She agrees to let him
live on the condition

00:04:05.536 --> 00:04:07.914
that he tells no
one what happened.

00:04:07.997 --> 00:04:09.499
She then walks
out of the shelter

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.626
disappearing into the blizzard.

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:14.379
A year later, Minokichi
meets a very beautiful woman

00:04:14.462 --> 00:04:17.548
who coincidentally also
has very pale skin.

00:04:17.632 --> 00:04:19.550
The two marry and
have 10 children.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:21.344
Clearly, they were
into each other.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:25.431
But strangely, she never seems
to age remaining as young

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:28.351
and beautiful as she was
on their wedding day.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.186
All was well until
one fateful night.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:33.815
Seeing his wife dressed
all in white Minokichi

00:04:33.898 --> 00:04:35.858
absentmindedly
comments that she looks

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:39.737
just like the snow woman he
encountered so many years ago.

00:04:39.821 --> 00:04:42.699
To his surprise and horror,
his wife reveals

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.867
she herself is the Yuki Onna.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:48.162
The wife turn on him,
furious.

00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:52.458
She screamed, "It was me
who spared you that day.

00:04:52.542 --> 00:04:55.420
I should kill you for
breaking your promise."

00:04:55.503 --> 00:04:57.922
(Emily)
She abandons him,
turning into a white mist

00:04:58.006 --> 00:05:00.842
and floating out of a window,
never to be seen again.

00:05:00.925 --> 00:05:02.719
This particular
Yuki Onna legend

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.262
is the most popular today

00:05:04.345 --> 00:05:08.474
largely because of Patrick
Hearn's 1904 translation

00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:10.518
of the story in
his book "Kwaidan."

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.186
This Irish Greek
author published

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:13.604
under a Japanese pen name

00:05:13.688 --> 00:05:15.440
and claimed to have
recorded the story

00:05:15.523 --> 00:05:18.067
from a local of the
Musashino district.

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:20.236
However, scholars are
careful to point out

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:23.239
that the story is unlikely
a direct translation.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.908
Romance between the Yuki Onna
and the young lumberjack

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.619
is significantly more
detailed in his telling

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:30.705
than in other variations.

00:05:30.788 --> 00:05:33.332
According to his version,
the Yuki Onna

00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:36.836
when disguised as a human
woman is named O-Yuki.

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:39.464
Her name literally
translates to snow,

00:05:39.547 --> 00:05:42.091
which you think would've been
a clue for the woodcutter.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.593
But I digress.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.846
The marriage element is common
in other Japanese folk tales.

00:05:46.929 --> 00:05:48.431
As is the husband
breaking a promise

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.308
to his supernatural wife.

00:05:50.391 --> 00:05:53.394
Other traditions across the
globe also use this trope

00:05:53.478 --> 00:05:54.687
so it's an interesting
thread to explore.

00:05:54.771 --> 00:05:57.607
These supernatural
unions seem to reflect

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.484
an idealistic fantasy.

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:02.695
The preternatural wife is
always incredibly attractive

00:06:02.779 --> 00:06:06.491
as defined by the ideal beauty
standards of that community.

00:06:06.574 --> 00:06:08.284
And Yuki Onna stories,
for instance,

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.495
female beauty is
defined by pale skin,

00:06:10.578 --> 00:06:12.455
long hair, and thinness.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.707
All characteristics
still held in high regard

00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:17.335
by popular culture
in Japan today.

00:06:17.418 --> 00:06:19.670
But Hiroko
has another opinion.

00:06:19.754 --> 00:06:22.381
I don't think portrayal
of Yuki Onna's beauty

00:06:22.465 --> 00:06:24.634
is about women at all.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:28.679
Instead, she's a personification
of the beauty of winter.

00:06:28.763 --> 00:06:31.516
She's like a
metaphor reminding us

00:06:31.599 --> 00:06:33.684
that the cold month
are beautiful,

00:06:33.768 --> 00:06:35.812
but it can also be deadly.

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:38.064
(Emily)
Another well-known
tale of the Yuki Onna

00:06:38.147 --> 00:06:40.608
that diverges from the
supernatural marriage trope

00:06:40.691 --> 00:06:42.985
appears in a 1705 play titled

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.696
"The Five Battledores
of the Yuki Onna."

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.574
Penned by Chikamatsu
Monzaemon, a noted kabuki

00:06:48.658 --> 00:06:49.909
and puppet theater playwright.

00:06:49.992 --> 00:06:52.995
He wrote both historical
and domestic dramas.

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.998
In other words, he wrote
about both legendary deeds

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:59.293
and heroic figures as well
as everyday domestic life.

00:06:59.377 --> 00:07:01.462
"The Five Battledores
of the Yuki Onna"

00:07:01.546 --> 00:07:03.923
falls somewhere in
between both categories.

00:07:04.006 --> 00:07:05.967
His version removes
the relationship

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:10.221
between yokai and man in favor
of a vengeful ghost story.

00:07:10.304 --> 00:07:12.723
The drama centers on a man
planning on assassinating

00:07:12.807 --> 00:07:15.810
a shogun in his home during
the New Year holiday.

00:07:15.893 --> 00:07:17.687
In order to do so,
he must get

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.939
the shogun's devoted
maid out of the house.

00:07:20.022 --> 00:07:21.691
So, he tells her that her boss

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:25.027
is planning to send an army to
fight the Lord of her lover.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.863
He instructs her to warn
the others in the household

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:29.490
ensuring the woman
that his brother

00:07:29.574 --> 00:07:31.242
is waiting outside
the garden gate

00:07:31.325 --> 00:07:32.702
to help her leave the property.

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:34.537
In truth, this is a lie.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.707
No one waits for her outside
the still locked gates

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.625
and the trapped maid
freezes to death

00:07:39.709 --> 00:07:42.003
inside the
snow-covered courtyard,

00:07:42.086 --> 00:07:44.172
but she does not
perish entirely.

00:07:44.255 --> 00:07:47.175
Upon her death, she
transforms into a snow woman.

00:07:47.258 --> 00:07:49.802
Her blue kimono replaced
with a white one.

00:07:49.886 --> 00:07:51.971
Then she seeks revenge
against the man

00:07:52.054 --> 00:07:54.140
who sent her on
the false errand.

00:07:54.223 --> 00:07:55.808
While the dangers of
being stuck outside

00:07:55.892 --> 00:07:58.644
on a snowy evening
are self-explanatory,

00:07:58.728 --> 00:08:01.480
this Yuki Onna tale also
warns of the consequences

00:08:01.564 --> 00:08:03.232
of trying to change
the social order

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:05.234
by usurping the leader
of the community,

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:06.903
in this case, the military.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:08.654
After all,
the would-be assassin

00:08:08.738 --> 00:08:11.240
is punished by the
vengeful snow woman.

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:13.993
But the fact that the maid
becomes the monster herself

00:08:14.076 --> 00:08:16.537
also suggests that
all lives are valuable.

00:08:16.621 --> 00:08:18.539
Even if a person
is not perceived

00:08:18.623 --> 00:08:20.666
as a high-ranking
member of society,

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.919
their lives are
no less important.

00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:26.255
While the dangers of frostbite
and hypothermia are universal

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:29.634
the minor changes in the
yokai's appearance and actions

00:08:29.717 --> 00:08:31.886
reflect regional
cultural expectations

00:08:31.969 --> 00:08:34.472
and potentially
real life events.

00:08:34.555 --> 00:08:36.974
(Hiroko)
She's popular character
in folk tales

00:08:37.058 --> 00:08:38.935
so they are many variations,

00:08:39.018 --> 00:08:43.397
but generally speaking, her
attributes don't change much.

00:08:43.481 --> 00:08:47.026
She's a beautiful
woman in a white kimono

00:08:47.109 --> 00:08:48.945
in the depth of winter.

00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:50.613
She reminds us of that,

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:53.282
but her story also tells us

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:57.036
never to make promises
we cannot keep.

00:08:58.287 --> 00:09:00.122
(Emily)
So there you have it,
and I mean, hey,

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:01.624
once you inspired a Pokemon

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:04.043
it's pretty hard to ignore
the pop culture relevance.

00:09:04.126 --> 00:09:06.671
What was once a metaphor
for the dangers of winter,

00:09:06.754 --> 00:09:09.340
and a warning against
false assurances of trust

00:09:09.423 --> 00:09:12.635
has become a beloved but
less terrifying character.

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:16.389
Expanding her reach,
but also her variation.

00:09:16.472 --> 00:09:18.683
What was once a metaphor
for the dangers of winter

00:09:18.766 --> 00:09:21.602
and a warning against false
insurances of trust...

00:09:23.145 --> 00:09:24.605
Assurances not insurances.

00:09:24.689 --> 00:09:25.982
Holy moley.

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:26.983
Assurances of--

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:28.317
(director)
Assurances.

00:09:28.401 --> 00:09:29.902
"Falsh ashurances."

00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:32.154
False assurances of trust.

